# Vercel builds only `landing` (project rootDirectory). Everything below is
# either rebuilt on the server or belongs to a different workspace, and
# uploading it made a CLI deploy push 1.6GB over the wire.
#
# ANCHOR ROOT-ONLY EXCLUDES WITH A LEADING SLASH.
# These patterns use .gitignore semantics: a bare name matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, not just the repo root. An unanchored
# `scripts` here excluded `landing/scripts/` too — which holds
# rename-shell.mjs, the `postbuild` step of the landing build. Every
# deploy from 2026-08-20 onward failed with
#   Command "npm ci && npm run build" exited with 1
# and, because landing had no deploy automation, nobody saw it: the
# share-link fix from 08-17 sat undeployed for two weeks while 48 real
# users' links stayed dead. Anchor anything meant for the root only.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Root-only workspaces — anchored, so a future landing/docs (etc.) is safe.
/mobile
/supabase
/docs
/store-assets

# (Removed: a bare `scripts`. There is no root-level scripts/ directory, so
# it excluded nothing intended while breaking the landing build. Do not
# reintroduce it unanchored.)

/.git
/.expo

# Build output at any depth — Vercel rebuilds it server-side, and shipping a
# stale local dist/ is worse than shipping none.
dist
build

*.log
